{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1507760-ashes-to-ashes-from-nobody-to-superghoul-in-5-years","id":1507760,"title":"Ashes to Ashes: from nobody to superghoul in 5 years?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-04-08T05:40:00-07:00","id":1507760,"title":"Ashes to Ashes: from nobody to superghoul in 5 years?","content":"We are given the stats of the Roarke the ghoul ( flashback ) in 1969 ( pg 62 of Ashes to Ashes for the date, pg 63 for the stats ).<br /> I'll not even start talking about the skills and attributes and limit the attention to his Disciplines: a single dot in Potence, Fortitude and Protean.<br /> Twenty years later, we are given the stats of Roarke the Villain: Fortitude 3, Potence 2, Obfuscate 4, Protean 4, Presence 1, Celerity 1, Domination 2.<br /> <br /> At page 8 we are said that Roarke found the body of a powerful Methuselah and ( pg 8 ) &quot;over the next half-decade, Roarke took time to build his base of power and master the abilities that the new Blood opened up to him&quot;.<br /> <br /> Basically Roarke learned a very minimum of 320 experience points worth of Disciplines in twenty years. Actually, we are explicitly told that he earned most of those in just the last five years. ( not to mention more or less 150 points of attributes, skills and specializations ).<br /> <br /> Now, I understood that Roarke was under the subconscious influence and mentoring of a very powerful vampire, but isn't such a boost simply ridiculous?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8595-conradine","name":"Conradine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8595_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-08T07:08:41-07:00","id":1507765,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Conradine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1507760-ashes-to-ashes-from-nobody-to-superghoul-in-5-years#post1507760\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now, I understood that Roarke was under the subconscious influence and mentoring of a very powerful vampire, but isn't such a boost simply ridiculous?</div> </div> </div> </div>The mentoring doesn't even account for anything, it's just fulfills the minimum requirement of learning disciplines for ghouls(they need a mentor to raise non-physical disciplines at all).<br /> <br /> Just chalk it up to the same weirdness that give multi millennia old vampires exponenially less XP than the average human couch potato. VTM has a very bad habit of giving stats to NPCs based entirely on what difficulty they want for the enemy scaling of a specific story and ignoring what makes sense for the lore entirely.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-08T09:33:26-07:00","id":1507770,"title":"","content":"To be fair, it's hard to criticise that particular case, since white wolf never even tried to give a general in universe rate of advancement for disciplines.<br /> <br /> All we can do is try to translate the equivalent of xp gain from game to the lore, but it rarely works with the npc given in the books.<br /> <br /> For exemple, you rarely see ancillae which even went to the 5th points of their clan disciplines. As if they didn't even tried to go to the full potential of their clan during a whole century...<br /> <br /> And it's no better for elder disciplines, most of the books says that powers between the 6th and 9th levels are often develloped over centuries, if not decades, but then you have mention of &quot;young vampires&quot; having special forms using the 8th level of protean.<br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b meaning they develloped it during their unlifetime, aka a few dozen years at most.<br /> <br /> <br /> So in short, it's impossible to have a set progression rate, so I'm hardly shocked by the superghoul in around 5 years.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","name":"Nyremne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-08T23:57:29-07:00","id":1507841,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Conradine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1507760-ashes-to-ashes-from-nobody-to-superghoul-in-5-years#post1507760\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now, I understood that Roarke was under the subconscious influence and mentoring of a very powerful vampire, but isn't such a boost simply ridiculous?</div> </div> </div> </div>In various works of art and media from time to time the authors do outline and create character who are exceptional and noteworthy. It happens in computer games, card games, and literature, as well. It can also happen that troublesome or problematic characters are included in a story.<br /> It has to be noted that it is a quality of RPG games that on many levels it is rather easy to ignore character who do not for some reason belong to your vision and idea of the setting.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-09T12:10:18-07:00","id":1507885,"title":"","content":"As <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1190-elphilm\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1190_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1190\" data-vbnamecard=\"1190\">Elphilm</a> said in the Followers of Set thread in the Werewolf forum, one of the things about the early WoD was that as soon as the books established a rule for the setting, there was always at least one writer ready to break that rule.<br /> <br /> I have no idea how &quot;old&quot; Ashes to Ashes is, but this sounds like that sort of thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3201-father-enoch","name":"Father Enoch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3201_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"285"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-09T13:38:13-07:00","id":1507896,"title":"","content":"The point is, 320 experience points worth of Disciplines in just 5 years is... it's simply too much. Under every standard.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8595-conradine","name":"Conradine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8595_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-09T14:23:02-07:00","id":1507897,"title":"","content":"I'm not trying to argue whether or not it's excessive.<br /> <br /> Rather, I'm speculating whether the author wrote it without realizing how excessive it may have been, or if they did this <i>because</i> it was excessive.<br /> <br /> They won't be the first or the last author to make a character who get powerful improbably fast. Some authors or characters are beloved for doing this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3201-father-enoch","name":"Father Enoch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3201_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"285"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-09T15:01:36-07:00","id":1507902,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyremne</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1507760-ashes-to-ashes-from-nobody-to-superghoul-in-5-years?p=1507770#post1507770\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be fair, it's hard to criticise that particular case, since white wolf never even tried to give a general in universe rate of advancement for disciplines.<br /> <br /> All we can do is try to translate the equivalent of xp gain from game to the lore, but it rarely works with the npc given in the books.<br /> <br /> For exemple, you rarely see ancillae which even went to the 5th points of their clan disciplines. As if they didn't even tried to go to the full potential of their clan during a whole century...<br /> <br /> And it's no better for elder disciplines, most of the books says that powers between the 6th and 9th levels are often develloped over centuries, if not decades, but then you have mention of &quot;young vampires&quot; having special forms using the 8th level of protean.<br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b meaning they develloped it during their unlifetime, aka a few dozen years at most.<br /> <br /> <br /> So in short, it's impossible to have a set progression rate, so I'm hardly shocked by the superghoul in around 5 years.</div> </div> </div> </div>These cases aren't anomalies?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-09T15:36:34-07:00","id":1507904,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Conradine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1507760-ashes-to-ashes-from-nobody-to-superghoul-in-5-years?p=1507896#post1507896\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The point is, 320 experience points worth of Disciplines in just 5 years is... it's simply too much. Under every standard.</div> </div> </div> </div>XP doesn't exist in-game. It's a purely out-of-character pacing mechanism.<br /> <br /> The game makes no distinction for how much XP you get over time. If my group plays once a week and earns an average of 4 XP a session, one player can get 208 XP in a year of play.<br /> <br /> If the pace of the story is roughly in keeping with real time, that means in five years, a PC could earn 1,040 XP.<br /> <br /> Spending a third of that on Disciplines doesn't seem so bad to me.<br /> <br /> Of course, the problem is the same amount of play could be a month, or a decade of in-game time to out-of-game time. If a year of player is 108 XP, but only a month has passed... five years of in-game time is well, more XP than you'd know what to do with. Obviously the other direction slows things down considerably.<br /> <br /> 320 XP worth of Disciplines in 5 years has no universal standard to actually compare it to. If you play in a lot of 1-to-1 time scale games, that's not really that exceptional. If you play in games were there's a much larger passage of time in-character compared to out of character, it feels more so.<br /> <br /> And of course, NPCs don't use XP unless they're ones the PCs can spend XP on to improve them directly. NPCs just have whatever stats the authors think is warranted.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-09T22:30:09-07:00","id":1507924,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Conradine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1507760-ashes-to-ashes-from-nobody-to-superghoul-in-5-years?p=1507896#post1507896\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The point is, 320 experience points worth of Disciplines in just 5 years is... it's simply too much. Under every standard.</div> </div> </div> </div>There is also the question of how did this character manage to achieve such a variety of powers. As far as I am aware each Discipline is like it's own topic and area of knowledge, symbolism, practice, and expertise. Drinking &quot;Vitae of an ancient Vampire&quot; only goes so far.<br /> <br /> At some point consistent effort through time and honest work - as well as definite knowledge comprehension and understanding - will definitely be required to progress in regard to development of special powers ( assuming that it is possible at all ) . Receiving regular tutelage and support might be another requirement.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-10T08:45:35-07:00","id":1507940,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Conradine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1507760-ashes-to-ashes-from-nobody-to-superghoul-in-5-years?p=1507896#post1507896\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The point is, 320 experience points worth of Disciplines in just 5 years is... it's simply too much. Under every standard.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not actually all that out there, a player who plays every day for a year following the 1 session = 1 night in game standard would earn 365+ XP easily.<br /> <br /> If you go by IRL examples of people going from skinny to bodybuilder in a few months(without steroids), IRL humans can average around 1 xp per week of dedicated effort on attributes. Thats not even counting the skills and knowledges they developed during that time.<br /> <br /> Honestly, 320 xp in 5 years isn't a stretch. VTM is just weirdly conservative giving XP to most old npcs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-10T10:22:14-07:00","id":1507945,"title":"","content":"Ashes to Ashes was a 1991 module that was published in first edition by what was a newly found company that, to my understanding, had a total sum experience of working in gaming of about 20 years.<br /> <br /> Is it going to have weirdness in it? Yes. Is it fair to point out the weirdness? Yes. Is it fair to criticize the weirdness? I would say No, for the reason above.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12895-mrnatas","name":"MrNatas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12895_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"180"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-10T19:54:34-07:00","id":1507990,"title":"","content":"Roarke is an awesome character in an awesome story. I run an adapted version of Ashes to Ashes recently and my players were awed by him, and the fact that was able to go toe to toe with Sheriff in the final fight. It helped to set the horror of the Methuselah sleeping in Chicago and made the PC's sympathize with an otherwise unsympathetic Lodin.<br /> If you need to stretch his powers a bit to make that impression, I think it's a great trade off. <br /> On the other hand you have Montreal by Night, where every Neonate had a boatload of disciplines for no good reason.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27429,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27429-microcuchon","user":"Microcuchon","date":". 04-10-2023, 10:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27429-microcuchon","name":"Microcuchon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"201"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-10T20:32:59-07:00","id":1507995,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Now, I understood that Roarke was under the subconscious influence and mentoring of a very powerful vampire, but isn't such a boost simply ridiculous? </div> </div> </div>Not at all, if it fits the story and if the story is good, all is forgiven. Most White Wolf characters don't follow this pattern of development dependent on time. You see many examples of 2 hundred years vampires with level 8-9 in disciplines (often in more than one), while at the same time you have cainites like Kritias from Chicago, who are thousand years old and have a ridiculous character sheet that any ragtag band of dirty fledglings could take him down.<br /> I don't care, if the story is good enough to hold itself, the rest is irrelevant.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12348,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","user":"Herr Meister","date":". 04-12-2023, 11:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}